    "title": "Cardano Founder Accuses Ethereum Co-Founder Of ‘Bag-Holding’ Over AI Cryptography Warning",
    "summary": "The post Cardano Founder Accuses Ethereum Co-Founder Of ‘Bag-Holding’ Over AI Cryptography Warning appeared first on Coinpedia Fintech News\nVitalik Buterin wants crypto to prepare for a threat that does not exist yet. Charles Hoskinson says that preparation could do more harm than the threat itself. On October 8, the Ethereum co-founder warned that AI-accelerated mathematics could break lattice-based cryptography, the backbone of the new post-quantum security standards. Within hours, the Cardano founder called …",
    "hasSummary": true,
    "link": "https://coinpedia.org/news/cardano-founder-accuses-ethereum-co-founder-of-bag-holding-over-ai-cryptography-warning/",
    "source": "Coinpedia",
    "tags": [
      "Cardano",
      "Ethereum",
      "Charles Hoskinson",
      "Vitalik Buterin"
    ],
    "origin": "rss",
    "pubDate": "2026-10-09T03:08:33.000Z",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-10-09T03:19:53.915Z",
    "isDuplicateOf": null,
    "content": "Cardano founder Charles Hoskinson has criticized Ethereum co-founder Vitalik Buterin over warnings about AI cryptography threats. Buterin recently claimed that AI-accelerated mathematics could undermine lattice-based cryptography, which forms the basis of new post-quantum security standards. Hoskinson argued that preparing for this unproven threat could cause more harm than the actual risk, sparking a fresh debate between the two prominent blockchain leaders.",
    "content_ta": "Ethereum co-founder Vitalik Buterin-ன் AI cryptography அச்சுறுத்தல்கள் பற்றிய எச்சரிக்கைக்கு Cardano founder Charles Hoskinson எதிர்ப்பு தெரிவித்துள்ளார். AI-accelerated கணிதம் எதிர்கால பாதுகாப்பு தரநிலைகளை பாதிக்கலாம் என்று Buterin எச்சரித்திருந்தார். ஆனால், இந்த வராத அச்சுறுத்தலுக்காக தயாராவது உண்மையான ஆபத்தை விட அதிக சேதத்தை ஏற்படுத்தும் என்று Hoskinson வாதிட்டுள்ளார்.",
    "slug": "cardano-founder-accuses-ethereum-co-founder-of-bag-holding-over-ai-cryptography-warning"
  },
